  "docs": {
    "description": "Icon-only action button. 126 variants: size (sm 32px, md 40px, lg 48px) × shape (square, round) × prio (primary, secondary, tertiary) × state (default, hover, active, pressed, focus, loading, disabled). Border and shadow match the Button variant of the same size, prio and state. Unlike Button, secondary and tertiary Icon Buttons keep a fill (action/{prio}/bg/{state}; none when disabled) so the glyph always sits on a surface. active is the persistent on state of a toggle icon button (e.g. a toolbar option switched on) — distinct from pressed, the momentary press; pressed keeps the control shadow, focus alone carries the ring. Drawn heights are the visible control; pad the hit area to 44×44 (size/target/min) in code. An icon-only control must carry an aria-label.",
    "figmaIssues": ["State axis has both `pressed` and `active`."]
  },
